+// WithOverrides returns a COPY of the encoder config carrying the per-room quality
+// a room creator chose (arcade per-room bitrate/FEC, threaded in via the t=104
+// GAME_START packet). It never mutates the shared config: List is a reference-type
+// map, so it is deep-copied before any CodecSettings.Params is rewritten — otherwise
+// one room's choice would leak into every concurrent room.
+//
+//	bitrateKbps > 0 → rewrite the ACTIVE video codec's `bitrate=` (kbps; nvh264enc/
+//	                  x264enc). Replace-only (clamped 500..20000 kbps) so vp8's
+//	                  `target-bitrate` is left alone.
+//	fec == 1        → force opus in-band FEC ON  (inband-fec=true,  packet-loss-percentage=15)
+//	fec == 2        → force opus in-band FEC OFF (inband-fec=false, packet-loss-percentage=0)
+//	fec == 0        → leave the opus params exactly as configured.
+func (e Encoder) WithOverrides(bitrateKbps int, fec int, codec string) Encoder {
+	codec = strings.ToLower(strings.TrimSpace(codec))
+	if codec == strings.ToLower(e.Video.Codec) {
+		codec = "" // no-op: already the active codec
